@baseUrl=http://localhost:8000/api/v1/deliveries
@deliveryId=REPLACE_WITH_DELIVERY_ID
@poolId=REPLACE_WITH_TARGET_REACHED_POOL_ID
@accessToken=REPLACE_WITH_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN

# See 00-smooth-flow.http for a chained run that gets a pool to
# TARGET_REACHED and creates a real delivery end to end — the DELIVERY_
# ASSIGNED notification only actually reaches anyone if the pool's offer
# resolves to a real supplier and/or the pool has real participants; an
# orphaned pool_ref silently notifies nobody (see notifications.http).

### create delivery (ADMIN only — pool must be TARGET_REACHED/DISTRIBUTING/COMPLETED, one per pool)
### Also raises the DELIVERY_ASSIGNED business event, which notifies the
### pool's supplier and every participating retailer — see notifications.http.

POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
    "pool_ref": "{{poolId}}"
}

### list deliveries (ADMIN sees all; RETAILER sees pools they joined; SUPPLIER sees pools built from their products)

GET {{baseUrl}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### get delivery by id

GET {{baseUrl}}/{{deliveryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### update delivery (ADMIN only)

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/{{deliveryId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
    "deliveryStatus": "DELIVERED"
}

### delete delivery (ADMIN only)

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{deliveryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
